WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:03.905
- If I ever hear my kids
say the word failure,

00:00:03.905 --> 00:00:06.148
I'd lock them in a room for a week.

00:00:06.148 --> 00:00:09.066
You've got to be able to
have a very clear vision

00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:10.203
of your business idea.

00:00:10.203 --> 00:00:13.639
Working out of 12 foot
by 12 foot was tough,

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.892
but when you happen to live there as well,

00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:16.946
it makes it that much harder.

00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:18.581
If a description of an entrepreneur is

00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:21.735
that I want to do it all
before I die, then I'm that.

00:00:21.735 --> 00:00:24.638
Research and feasibility
are fundamentally important

00:00:24.638 --> 00:00:26.126
when starting a new business.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.093
A new business venture
will require the majority

00:00:28.093 --> 00:00:30.790
of your time, effort and dedication.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:35.455
I'd actually say that for an
entrepreneur this is the time.

00:00:35.455 --> 00:00:38.175
So many people talk about doing something

00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:39.719
or say, "What if?".

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:43.172
Successful entrepreneurs have
two undeniable qualities,

00:00:43.172 --> 00:00:45.173
determination and persistence.

00:00:45.173 --> 00:00:46.847
I don't have to work 16 hours a day,

00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:49.318
I love working 16 hours a day.

00:00:49.318 --> 00:00:52.357
- He's a British entrepreneur
with interest in media,

00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:54.905
mobile phones leisure and property.

00:00:54.905 --> 00:00:57.160
He was appointed Commander of the Order

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.358
of the British Empire in 2009.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:03.108
His estimated networth
is 475 million pounds.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.759
He's Peter Jones and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:10.995
(wooshing and detonation booming)

00:01:10.995 --> 00:01:12.331
- I mean I've got a real belief

00:01:12.331 --> 00:01:13.981
and this is a true belief

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:15.071
and those of you,

00:01:15.071 --> 00:01:17.141
everybody's got kids out there,

00:01:17.141 --> 00:01:20.441
if I ever hear my kids
say the word failure,

00:01:20.441 --> 00:01:24.122
I'd lock them in a room for a week.

00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:27.563
I would request if we have
any power in this country

00:01:27.563 --> 00:01:29.900
that we could take that out
of our English dictionary

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.061
and replace it with the word feedback.

00:01:32.061 --> 00:01:35.292
Because that's all failure
in our words is, isn't it?

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:37.444
It's feedback, we learn from mistakes.

00:01:37.444 --> 00:01:40.326
You've got to be able to
have a very clear vision

00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:42.562
of your business idea.

00:01:42.562 --> 00:01:45.639
Without it you won't actually
know where you're going.

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:48.197
So in the year 2000 I
set up Generation Telecom

00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:50.183
and Generation Telecom was a business

00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:54.289
that supplied airtime to the rail users.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:57.544
I believe that I could set
up and manage this business

00:01:57.544 --> 00:01:59.851
and within two or three years sell out

00:01:59.851 --> 00:02:01.479
to the major networks.

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:03.811
Well, within three years
we successfully sold it

00:02:03.811 --> 00:02:06.521
to Vodafone making millions of pounds.

00:02:06.521 --> 00:02:09.013
But without that vision at the outset,

00:02:09.013 --> 00:02:12.687
my business would not have
gone the way that it did.

00:02:12.687 --> 00:02:16.140
I started my Telecom's business in 1998

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.072
and today it's one of the
most successful businesses

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.072
of its kind.

00:02:23.754 --> 00:02:27.921
It generates income about a
150 million pounds per annum.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.696
All companies have to start somewhere

00:02:32.696 --> 00:02:34.506
and my business actually started

00:02:34.506 --> 00:02:37.489
in a tiny little office in Slough.

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:41.249
Starting the business was a
pretty terrifying experience.

00:02:41.249 --> 00:02:42.978
Every single penny that I had went

00:02:42.978 --> 00:02:45.347
into starting the business.

00:02:45.347 --> 00:02:48.730
But it kind of gave me a real edge,

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.117
it gave me the sheer determination

00:02:50.117 --> 00:02:52.301
that actually I can do this.

00:02:52.301 --> 00:02:54.728
And as each day and each week passed

00:02:54.728 --> 00:02:56.813
when you get more and more opportunities,

00:02:56.813 --> 00:02:58.873
more and more money
comes into the business,

00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:00.259
it becomes even more exciting.

00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:03.304
(guitar music)

00:03:03.304 --> 00:03:04.472
The size of the office that I worked

00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:08.362
from when I started
was 12 foot by 12 foot.

00:03:08.362 --> 00:03:11.631
Working out of 12 foot
by 12 foot was tough.

00:03:11.631 --> 00:03:13.649
But when you happen to live there as well,

00:03:13.649 --> 00:03:16.066
it makes it that much harder.

00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:18.928
And what was quite interesting,

00:03:18.928 --> 00:03:20.724
there were even employees in the company

00:03:20.724 --> 00:03:23.870
that didn't know that I
was staying and sleeping

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.953
and living in the office.

00:03:28.355 --> 00:03:32.017
Now, there are a few things
that I learned personally.

00:03:32.017 --> 00:03:34.095
One was a sheer determination.

00:03:34.095 --> 00:03:37.286
Number two was never giving up

00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:40.539
and number three was to
be results orientated.

00:03:40.539 --> 00:03:41.478
I had to get results,

00:03:41.478 --> 00:03:44.895
if I wanted to get my life back on track.

00:03:45.831 --> 00:03:48.014
I've been on an amazing
journey since then,

00:03:48.014 --> 00:03:52.416
but I will never ever forget
those real, real tough days.

00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:55.987
To be perfectly honest I'm a
little bit confused myself.

00:03:55.987 --> 00:03:57.432
One minute I'm running a business,

00:03:57.432 --> 00:03:59.164
next minute I'm investing in one,

00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:01.446
the next minute I'm seeing
some crazy people come

00:04:01.446 --> 00:04:04.750
and pitch me a toilet snake
idea from Dragon's Den.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.482
Then I'm walking down the
BAFTA's or the Red Carpet Awards

00:04:08.482 --> 00:04:09.392
and then I'm now trying

00:04:09.392 --> 00:04:11.196
to build a National Enterprise Academy,

00:04:11.196 --> 00:04:14.489
so I think if a description
of an entrepreneur is

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:18.241
that I want to do it all
before I die, then I'm that.

00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:20.259
You need to research your idea,

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:22.481
so that you've covered off
not just all the competition

00:04:22.481 --> 00:04:25.854
in the market, but you've
checked and double checked

00:04:25.854 --> 00:04:29.915
whether your idea is
likely to work or not.

00:04:29.915 --> 00:04:32.056
So many people today start up a business

00:04:32.056 --> 00:04:34.455
because they do it on a back of a whim.

00:04:34.455 --> 00:04:36.322
They need to research the market,

00:04:36.322 --> 00:04:38.093
they need to discuss how feasible it is

00:04:38.093 --> 00:04:39.870
and then ask questions.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.690
How am I going to get out of the business?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.067
Whom I'm going to sell it to?

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:44.948
Who are the competitors in the market?

00:04:44.948 --> 00:04:46.573
Who are my suppliers?

00:04:46.573 --> 00:04:48.499
How much money do I need
to start the business?

00:04:48.499 --> 00:04:50.126
How will I market the company?

00:04:50.126 --> 00:04:52.132
There's a lot to consider.

00:04:52.132 --> 00:04:55.290
But research and feasibility
are fundamentally important

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.088
when starting a new business.

00:04:57.088 --> 00:04:58.838
Number six is timing.

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:01.844
Supportive partners, circumstances

00:05:01.844 --> 00:05:05.487
and good health are all what I
call critical success factors

00:05:05.487 --> 00:05:07.332
when starting a new business.

00:05:07.332 --> 00:05:09.609
A new business venture
will require the majority

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:12.576
of your time, effort and dedication.

00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:15.438
Times like this are very difficult.

00:05:15.438 --> 00:05:19.717
But I'm going to be a little bit
controversial and actually say

00:05:19.717 --> 00:05:23.712
that for an entrepreneur this is the time.

00:05:23.712 --> 00:05:25.823
And there are many
entrepreneurs that I speak to

00:05:25.823 --> 00:05:26.906
that are out there, that are saying,

00:05:26.906 --> 00:05:30.812
"You know what, I'm
pleased this has happened.

00:05:30.812 --> 00:05:34.055
This is a time for me now to step up.

00:05:34.055 --> 00:05:38.469
This is a time for my business
to really go up to the plate.

00:05:38.469 --> 00:05:41.411
This is the time where the competition

00:05:41.411 --> 00:05:45.578
that was out there, that wasn't
that good is disappearing."

00:05:46.665 --> 00:05:50.165
Recession in my mind can drive innovation.

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:53.963
And the reason for that quite simply is

00:05:53.963 --> 00:05:56.760
because we can do more with less.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.771
We are forced to do more with less.

00:05:58.771 --> 00:06:00.525
Take action.

00:06:00.525 --> 00:06:03.296
So many people talk about doing something

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.384
or say, "What if?".

00:06:05.384 --> 00:06:08.137
They don't actually get up and do it.

00:06:08.137 --> 00:06:11.207
Taking action is really, really important.

00:06:11.207 --> 00:06:14.561
In 1998 when I was working
for another company

00:06:14.561 --> 00:06:15.682
I was umming and ahhing

00:06:15.682 --> 00:06:17.833
of whether to set up my own business.

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.388
I didn't have a lot of money,

00:06:20.388 --> 00:06:23.727
but I decided to take action
and I decided to do it.

00:06:23.727 --> 00:06:25.145
But I did it in a very planned way,

00:06:25.145 --> 00:06:27.137
I knew exactly what I was going to do,

00:06:27.137 --> 00:06:29.685
I knew exactly what I wanted to achieve,

00:06:29.685 --> 00:06:32.781
but the most important
thing, I took action.

00:06:32.781 --> 00:06:36.721
Within two or three years
I was a millionaire again.

00:06:36.721 --> 00:06:38.519
Probably the best thing that I ever did.

00:06:38.519 --> 00:06:40.956
So taking action is absolutely vital.

00:06:40.956 --> 00:06:44.588
Successful entrepreneurs have
two undeniable qualities,

00:06:44.588 --> 00:06:47.054
determination and persistence.

00:06:47.054 --> 00:06:50.662
Develop a keep-on-keeping-on
ability to be called upon

00:06:50.662 --> 00:06:52.101
whenever you might need it.

00:06:52.101 --> 00:06:53.502
Well, you get things like this

00:06:53.502 --> 00:06:56.111
because being blunt
I've worked bloody hard,

00:06:56.111 --> 00:06:58.969
I wasn't born with a
silver spoon in my mouth.

00:06:58.969 --> 00:07:00.096
And that's the great thing

00:07:00.096 --> 00:07:01.602
that my life has given me now.

00:07:01.602 --> 00:07:03.382
It's that it gives me freedom

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:05.089
and it gives me choice.

00:07:05.089 --> 00:07:07.741
I can choose what I want to
do, when I want to do it.

00:07:07.741 --> 00:07:09.374
I don't have to work 16 hours a day,

00:07:09.374 --> 00:07:11.660
I love working 16 hours a day

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.487
because I enjoy what I do.

00:07:14.487 --> 00:07:15.456
I get asked a lot,

00:07:15.456 --> 00:07:18.130
"Do you really appreciate
what you've got?".

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:18.963
I know what it's like

00:07:18.963 --> 00:07:20.220
to have everything and love everything,

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.825
so I'm not mister take-it-for-granted.

00:07:22.825 --> 00:07:25.772
I cherish what I have,
I'm lucky to have it,

00:07:25.772 --> 00:07:27.892
but boy, do I make good use of it.

00:07:27.892 --> 00:07:29.355
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:07:29.355 --> 00:07:32.616
I made this video because
Amin Abdul asked me to.

00:07:32.616 --> 00:07:33.720
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.864
that you want me to profile next,

00:07:35.864 --> 00:07:37.051
leave in the comments below

00:07:37.051 --> 00:07:37.884
and I will see what I can do.

00:07:37.884 --> 00:07:38.717
I'd also love to know

00:07:38.717 --> 00:07:42.049
which of Peter Jones's top 10
rules meant the most to you,

00:07:42.049 --> 00:07:43.476
had the biggest impact.

00:07:43.476 --> 00:07:44.309
Leave it in the comments,

00:07:44.309 --> 00:07:45.364
I'm enjoying the discussion.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.562
Thank you so much for watching.

00:07:46.562 --> 00:07:49.445
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:07:49.445 --> 00:07:52.081
(wooshing and detonation booming)

